# ===========================================================================
# BitArchive
#
# Desktop-first emulation frontend built on Rust + Slint + SQLite,
# organized as a Cargo workspace.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   Cargo.lock  -  BitArchive builds a binary/desktop target, so the lockfile
#                  is committed to keep builds reproducible.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Rust / Cargo build output ---------------------------------------------
target/
*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.profraw

# --- Slint -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Slint compiles .slint sources into Rust inside Cargo's OUT_DIR (which lives
# under target/), so no generated sources appear in the working tree.

# --- Local runtime state / SQLite ------------------------------------------
# The SQLite database is local user state, not source. Test fixtures should be
# placed under tests/ and force-added if they genuinely need to be tracked.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# --- Environment and secrets -----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
secrets.json

# --- Logs and local scratch ------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
tmp/
scratch/
*.local

# --- Managed component store / downloaded runtime artifacts ----------------
# Runtime and core components are downloaded into the application data
# directories (ARCHITECTURE.md §23.1, §35) and are never source. The patterns
# below only catch a component store that was deliberately rooted inside the
# repository during local development; they must never be used to commit a
# runtime, a core, a ROM, or firmware.
components/
artifacts/
*.dmg
*_libretro.dylib

# --- Local test content: ROMs, disc images, firmware -----------------------
# Content and firmware are user-owned external files (AGENTS.md §4) and this
# repository is public: a game image, a disc image, or a firmware dump must never
# be committed here. The directories are where the developer vertical slice keeps
# local verification content at the repository root; the extensions are a backstop
# for a file dropped next to the sources.
#
# Ambiguous extensions are deliberately absent: `*.md` is Markdown in this
# repository (even though it is also a Mega Drive ROM extension) and `*.bin` is
# too ambiguous to claim. A test fixture that genuinely needs tracking belongs
# under `tests/` and is force-added, as the local-state section notes.
/ROMS/
/BIOS/
*.gba
*.gb
*.gbc
*.nes
*.fds
*.sfc
*.smc
*.iso
*.cue
*.chd

# --- Test / coverage output ------------------------------------------------
coverage/

# --- macOS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- IDE / editor ----------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
